-- Employment Claims Act 2016 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: PART 4, MISCELLANEOUS (ss 28 to 35).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively.  Target compiler: main (build 109).
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE is a yes the Act gives; JUST FALSE is a no the Act gives in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered" (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- s 32 (amending the Schedules), s 33 (Rules of Court), s 34 (regulations) and s 35(1) (issuing guidelines) are powers to make instruments: machinery (inert, reason 2).
-- What the Rules of Court or regulations say is asked, where a rule turns on it, as a MAYBE input.

§ `Part 4 -- Miscellaneous`

§§ `s 28 -- restriction on contracting out`

-- s 28: it does not matter when the agreement was made.
-- src:1813 | 28. Any provision in any agreement (whether made before, on or
-- src:1814 | after 1 April 2017) is void to the extent that it purports —
@ref s 28 (src:1813-1814)
GIVEN `the date on which the agreement was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28 the date on which the agreement was made does not affect whether the provision is void` MEANS
    -- "whether made before, on or after 1 April 2017": every date gives the same answer, so the date is read and not used
    JUST TRUE

-- s 28: a provision in an agreement is void to the extent that it purports to exclude or limit a tribunal's jurisdiction, or to prevent a person from submitting a mediation request or making a claim, application or appeal under this Act.
-- src:1813 | 28. Any provision in any agreement (whether made before, on or
-- src:1814 | after 1 April 2017) is void to the extent that it purports —
-- src:1816 | (a) to exclude or limit the jurisdiction of a tribunal; or
-- src:1818 | (b) to prevent a person from —
-- src:1820 | (i) submitting a mediation request; or
-- src:1822 | (ii) making a claim, an application or an appeal under
-- src:1823 | this Act.
@ref s 28 (src:1813-1823)
GIVEN purports IS A `What a provision of an agreement purports to do`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28 the provision in the agreement is void to that extent` MEANS
    CONSIDER purports
    WHEN `Exclude or limit the jurisdiction of a tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Prevent a person from submitting a mediation request` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `Prevent a person from making a claim, an application or an appeal under this Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [open question; reviewer expected JUST FALSE]: the provision is void "to the extent that it purports" to do one of the things named; what else it purports to do is not spoken to
    WHEN `Something else` THEN NOTHING

§§ `s 29 -- disclosure of information`

-- s 29(3): "law enforcement agency" means any authority or person charged with the duty of investigating offences or charging offenders under any written law.
-- src:1859 | (3) In this section —
-- src:1861 | “law enforcement agency” means any authority or person
-- src:1862 | charged with the duty of investigating offences or charging
-- src:1863 | offenders under any written law;
@ref s 29(3) “law enforcement agency” (src:1859-1863)
GIVEN `it is an authority or person charged with the duty of investigating offences or charging offenders under any written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(3) the body is a law enforcement agency` MEANS
    IF `it is an authority or person charged with the duty of investigating offences or charging offenders under any written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“law enforcement agency” means any authority or person charged with the duty of investigating offences or charging offenders under any written law"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 29(3): "public agency" means (a) the Government, including any ministry, department, agency or Organ of State; or (b) any statutory body or tribunal prescribed for the purposes of the definition.
-- src:1865 | “public agency” means —
-- src:1867 | (a) the Government, including any ministry, department,
-- src:1868 | agency or Organ of State; or
-- src:1870 | (b) any statutory body or tribunal that is prescribed for
-- src:1871 | the purposes of this definition by any regulations
-- src:1872 | made under section 34.
@ref s 29(3) “public agency” (src:1865-1872)
GIVEN `it is the Government, including a ministry, department, agency or Organ of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a statutory body or tribunal prescribed for the purposes of this definition by regulations made under section 34` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(3) the body is a public agency` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is the Government, including a ministry, department, agency or Organ of State` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `it is a statutory body or tribunal prescribed for the purposes of this definition by regulations made under section 34` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): which statutory bodies or tribunals are prescribed is in regulations that are not among the sources
        IF `it is a statutory body or tribunal prescribed for the purposes of this definition by regulations made under section 34` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“public agency” means (a) the Government ...; or (b) any statutory body or tribunal that is prescribed"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 29(1): the Commissioner, an approved mediator, a tribunal magistrate or a Registrar may disclose information relating to a mediation request, a mediation under Part 2, a claim or any proceedings before a tribunal, if the disclosure meets one of (a) to (f).
-- src:1827 | 29.—(1) Despite sections 4 and 18, the Commissioner, an approved
-- src:1828 | mediator, a tribunal magistrate or a Registrar may disclose
-- src:1829 | information relating to a mediation request, a mediation under
-- src:1830 | Part 2, a claim or any proceedings before a tribunal, if the
-- src:1831 | disclosure —
-- src:1833 | (a) is necessary for or in connection with the administration or
-- src:1834 | execution of this Act;
-- src:1836 | (b) is necessary for providing financial or social assistance to
-- src:1837 | the claimant or the respondent;
-- src:1842 | (c) is made to assist a law enforcement agency in the
-- src:1843 | investigation of any offence under any written law;
-- src:1845 | (d) is made to a public agency for the purpose of policy
-- src:1846 | formulation or review;
-- src:1848 | (e) is made to a public agency, and is necessary in the public
-- src:1849 | interest; or
-- src:1851 | (f) is made for any other purpose that may be prescribed by
-- src:1852 | any regulations made under section 34.
@ref s 29(1) (src:1827-1852)
GIVEN discloser IS A `Person who may disclose under section 29`
      `the disclosure is necessary for or in connection with the administration or execution of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is necessary for providing financial or social assistance to the claimant or the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made to assist a law enforcement agency in the investigation of an offence under any written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made to a public agency for the purpose of policy formulation or review` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made to a public agency and is necessary in the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is made for another purpose prescribed by regulations made under section 34` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(1) the person may disclose the information` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the permission is given to "the Commissioner, an approved mediator, a tribunal magistrate or a Registrar"; the clause names who may disclose and carries no "only"
        IF discloser EQUALS `Someone else who holds information` THEN NOTHING
        IF `the disclosure is necessary for or in connection with the administration or execution of this Act` OR `the disclosure is necessary for providing financial or social assistance to the claimant or the respondent` OR `the disclosure is made to assist a law enforcement agency in the investigation of an offence under any written law` OR `the disclosure is made to a public agency for the purpose of policy formulation or review` OR `the disclosure is made to a public agency and is necessary in the public interest` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the disclosure is made for another purpose prescribed by regulations made under section 34` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): purpose (f) is "any other purpose prescribed by regulations made under section 34", and whether one is prescribed for this disclosure is not among the sources
        IF `the disclosure is made for another purpose prescribed by regulations made under section 34` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may disclose information ... if the disclosure is — (a) ... (f) for any other purpose prescribed by regulations" (the disclosure meets none of the purposes)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 29(2): a tribunal magistrate or a Registrar may publish information relating to an order or a decision of a tribunal.
-- src:1854 | (2) Despite section 18, a tribunal magistrate or a Registrar may
-- src:1855 | publish information relating to an order or a decision of a tribunal.
@ref s 29(2) (src:1854-1855)
GIVEN discloser IS A `Person who may disclose under section 29`
      `the information relates to an order or a decision of a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 29(2) the person may publish the information` MEANS
    IF (discloser EQUALS `A tribunal magistrate` OR discloser EQUALS `A Registrar`) AND `the information relates to an order or a decision of a tribunal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: the permission is for "a tribunal magistrate or a Registrar" and for "information relating to an order or a decision of a tribunal"
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `ss 30 and 31 -- protection and public servants`

-- s 30(1): a tribunal magistrate has the same protection as a Magistrate has under the State Courts Act 1970.
-- src:1876 | 30.—(1) A tribunal magistrate has and enjoys the same protection
-- src:1877 | that a Magistrate has and enjoys under the State Courts Act 1970.
@ref s 30(1) (src:1876-1877)
GIVEN `the person is a tribunal magistrate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(1) the person has the same protection that a Magistrate has under the State Courts Act 1970` MEANS
    IF `the person is a tribunal magistrate`
    -- (what that protection is lies in the State Courts Act 1970, which is not among the sources)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [scope limit, ruled (c)]: "A tribunal magistrate has and enjoys the same protection"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 30(2): a Registrar, when exercising the jurisdiction and powers of a tribunal, has the same protection as a tribunal magistrate.
-- src:1879 | (2) A Registrar, when exercising the jurisdiction and powers of a
-- src:1880 | tribunal, has and enjoys the same protection as a tribunal magistrate.
@ref s 30(2) (src:1879-1880)
GIVEN `the person is a Registrar exercising the jurisdiction and powers of a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(2) the Registrar has the same protection as a tribunal magistrate` MEANS
    IF `the person is a Registrar exercising the jurisdiction and powers of a tribunal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A Registrar, when exercising the jurisdiction and powers of a tribunal" [assumed: when] (the input states the Registrar and the exercise together; false is read as the exercise not being under way)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 30(3): no liability lies personally against the Commissioner, an individual authorised to carry out a function or duty of the Commissioner, or an approved mediator, who acts in good faith and with reasonable care.
-- src:1882 | (3) No liability shall lie personally against the Commissioner, an
-- src:1883 | individual authorised to carry out any function or duty of the
-- src:1884 | Commissioner under this Act, or an approved mediator, who, acting
-- src:1885 | in good faith and with reasonable care, does or omits to do anything in
-- src:1886 | the execution or purported execution of this Act.
@ref s 30(3) (src:1882-1886)
GIVEN person IS A `Person protected under section 30(3)`
      `the person acted in good faith and with reasonable care in doing or omitting to do the thing, in the execution or purported execution of this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 30(3) no liability lies personally against the person` MEANS
    IF person EQUALS `Someone else`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [open question; reviewer expected JUST FALSE]: the protection is for "the Commissioner, an individual authorised ..., or an approved mediator"
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the person acted in good faith and with reasonable care in doing or omitting to do the thing, in the execution or purported execution of this Act`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording) [open question; reviewer expected JUST FALSE]: "who, acting in good faith and with reasonable care"; a person who did not so act is not within the protection and the text does not say that liability lies
         ELSE NOTHING

-- s 31(1): an approved mediator carrying out the functions and duties of an approved mediator is deemed a public servant for the purposes of the Penal Code 1871.
-- src:1893 | 31.—(1) Every approved mediator, when carrying out the functions
-- src:1894 | and duties of an approved mediator, is deemed to be a public servant
-- src:1895 | for the purposes of the Penal Code 1871.
@ref s 31(1) (src:1893-1895)
GIVEN `the person is an approved mediator carrying out the functions and duties of an approved mediator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(1) the approved mediator is deemed to be a public servant for the purposes of the Penal Code 1871` MEANS
    IF `the person is an approved mediator carrying out the functions and duties of an approved mediator`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when carrying out the functions and duties of an approved mediator" [assumed: when] (the input states the mediator and the carrying out together; false is read as the carrying out not being under way)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 31(2): an authorised person carrying out a function or duty of the Commissioner under this Act is deemed a public servant for the purposes of the Penal Code 1871.
-- src:1897 | (2) Every authorised person, when carrying out any function or
-- src:1898 | duty of the Commissioner under this Act, is deemed to be a public
-- src:1899 | servant for the purposes of the Penal Code 1871.
@ref s 31(2) (src:1897-1899)
GIVEN `the person is an authorised person carrying out a function or duty of the Commissioner under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 31(2) the authorised person is deemed to be a public servant for the purposes of the Penal Code 1871` MEANS
    IF `the person is an authorised person carrying out a function or duty of the Commissioner under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "when carrying out any function or duty of the Commissioner under this Act" [assumed: when] (the input states the person and the carrying out together; false is read as the carrying out not being under way)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 35(2) -- the tripartite guidelines on wrongful dismissal`

-- s 35(2): upon the publication of the guidelines in the Gazette, regard may be had to them for the purposes of sections 20(7) and 25(4).
-- src:2124 | (2) Upon the publication of those guidelines in the Gazette, regard
-- src:2125 | may be had to those guidelines for the purposes of sections 20(7) and
-- src:2126 | 25(4).
@ref s 35(2) (src:2124-2126)
GIVEN `the guidelines have been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 35(2) regard may be had to the guidelines for the purposes of sections 20(7) and 25(4)` MEANS
    IF `the guidelines have been published in the Gazette`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the publication of those guidelines in the Gazette" [assumed: when] (they are not yet published)
    ELSE JUST FALSE
